#paragraph_tab
The preliminaries are the materials that this book will use directly and repeatedly. By contrast, the present chapter is a place for optional explanations, geometric intuition, coordinate computations, and side remarks that may help the reader build a better picture of the subject.

#paragraph_tab
Therefore, it is completely acceptable to skip this chapter at first reading and return to it only when some topic feels unfamiliar. The goal is not to add more prerequisites, but to provide a separate place for helpful background that should not interrupt the main line of study.

#paragraph_tab
As this book grows, this chapter can collect optional topics such as additional examples, intuitive interpretations, and short reviews of related ideas that are useful but not strictly necessary.
